The user wants a layout component with two variants (full-width and centered) using Tailwind CSS. I'll create a clean, reusable React component with TypeScript support, proper variants, and good documentation. Let me design this thoughtfully with a polished visual demo.# Layout Component with Tailwind CSS

Here's a flexible, reusable layout component with `full-width` and `centered` variants, plus a live demo showing both in action.

## The Component

```tsx
import React from "react";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"; // or your className merge helper

type LayoutProps = {
  variant?: "full-width" | "centered";
  as?: React.ElementType;
  className?: string;
  children: React.ReactNode;
};

export function Layout({
  variant = "centered",
  as: Component = "section",
  className,
  children,
}: LayoutProps) {
  return (
    <Component
      className={cn(
        "w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8",
        variant === "centered" && "mx-auto max-w-7xl",
        className
      )}
    >
      {children}
    </Component>
  );
}
```

## Usage

```tsx
// Centered (default) — constrained to max-w-7xl
<Layout>
  <h1>Centered content</h1>
</Layout>

// Full-width — spans the entire viewport
<Layout variant="full-width">
  <h1>Full-width content</h1>
</
